  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The Figure of Knowledge shows clear signs of use and reach for a scholarly book in architectural theory: it has 2,817 recorded downloads and is available in open form through multiple repository instances. The record also shows institutional support from KU Leuven, while citation evidence is still at an early stage with no citations indexed in OpenAlex.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Published by Leuven University Press in 2020, The Figure of Knowledge contributes a critical historiography of architectural theory, with library subject indexing placing it at the intersection of modern architecture, historiography, philosophy, and the modern movement in architecture. The book is openly accessible in the record, which likely supports its visibility and practical use among readers working in these areas.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The strongest impact signal is sustained usage: OAPEN metrics report 2,817 downloads, indicating that the book has been actively consulted. Monthly download data show continued engagement across the reporting period rather than a single isolated spike, suggesting the work has maintained reader interest over time.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The scholarly uptake record remains limited at present, with zero citations indexed in OpenAlex. That does not diminish the book\u2019s relevance, but it does mean the available evidence currently points more clearly to readership and access than to documented citation-based influence.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Additional signals support the book\u2019s circulation and adoption potential. OpenAlex lists three authors, and the record includes two library holdings in Open Library, alongside WorldCat subject coverage that aligns with teaching and research in architecture and historiography. A peer-review signal is also registered in the open-science record, and the book is associated with KU Leuven funding support.</p>",
